7961 0 obj
  << /ActualText (If the there are more letters than numbers in the SN do the following but only to routes    or    \072\n\050\023 If the graph left to the diamond square as a first \n  step indicates to ignore the left two paths\054 flip the \n  last instruction if it\031s of the same type\n\023 Else add that first step as is to the end of \n  route \n\nIf there are less letters than numbers in the SN do the following but only to route    \072\n\n\023 If the graph on the right last step matches the first  \n  step of the current route add it to the beginning\056\n\023 Else add it as an extra last step\056\n\nA step type is of the same type even if it\031s mirrored\056\nAlways round down when dividing\056\050\nIf the SN ends with the number 1\054 3\054 5\054 7 or 9 find the first digit in the SN\054 divide it by 2 and add it to the solution\056\n\nIf the SN ends with the number 0\054 2\054 4\054 6 or 8 find the first digit in the SN\054 divide it by 2 and subtract it from the solution\056\n\nIf the SN ends with a letter\054 add up all route numbers seen and divide by the amount of numbers seen and round down\054 this digit replaces the solution\056\n\nFor the    route add the fourth number of the SN divided by 2 to the solution\nFor the    route add the third number of the SN divided by 2 to the solution\nFor the    route add the second number of the SN divided by 2 to the solution\nFor the    route add the first number of the SN divided by 2 to the solution\nIf such a number does not exist\054 ignore it\056\n\nThe solution can never be less than one\054 it then instead becomes one\056)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 7962 0 R
     /Pg 4781 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

7962 0 obj
  << /K [ 7961 0 R ]
     /P 7993 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 4781 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

