7991 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Preservation systems rely on layered routing structures that must remain aligned under fluctuating operational conditions\056\n\nLayered routings utilize graphical calibration panels for active adjustment\056 Similar panels are used in regions deployed during initial planetary colonization\056 These panels simulate distributed path configurations and require careful interpretation before intervention\056\050\nPrimary reference panels are typically located east of the central deployed structure core and mounted within communal command displays used for crew orientation and systems briefings\056 These surfaces feature repeating geometric icons and are designed to test spatial reasoning\054 pattern recognition\054 and structural discipline under controlled conditions\056\n\nSuccessful alignment demonstrates readiness for more intricate Preservation environments\056)
     /K [ 22 ]
     /P 7992 0 R
     /Pg 4781 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

